# Report whether a user unit is active. This program only reads state; starting,
# stopping or enabling a unit is an effectful separate program.
# Run with: execute examples/desktop/systemd-user.program --input unit=app.service
accept unit as text

run systemd.user.is_active with unit unit as reply and keep status as code
take text at "/outcome" from reply as state
if state is "active"
  run "printf" with arguments ["%s is active\n", unit]
otherwise
  run "printf" with arguments ["%s is %s\n", unit, state]
